 **Data Structures and Layout:**
 *   **Texture $I$ (RGB Triplets):** A 3D texture storing the indices and mean values [S1, unofficial]. The dimensions are $D_x' \times D_y' \times D_z'$, where $D_x' = D_x/4$, $D_y' = D_y/4$, and $D_z' = D_z/4$ [S1, unofficial]. Each texel contains three components: $r$ (8-bit index for Codebook A), $g$ (8-bit index for Codebook B), and $b$ (mean value) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Texture $C_a$ (Codebook A):** A 2D texture storing difference vectors for 4x4x4 blocks [S1, unofficial]. Dimensions are $256 \times 64$. The $s$-coordinate corresponds to the index in $I.r$, and the $w$-coordinate (0–63) corresponds to the local position within the 4x4x4 block [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Texture $C_b$ (Codebook B):** A 2D texture storing detail vectors for 2x2x2 blocks [S1, unofficial]. Dimensions are $256 \times 8$. The $s$-coordinate corresponds to the index in $I.g$, and the $w$-coordinate (0–7) corresponds to the local position within the 2x2x2 block [S1, unofficial].
