 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per voxel, as decoding involves a constant number of texture lookups and arithmetic operations [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is determined by the size of the compressed data: $D_x' D_y' D_z'$ triplets for indices/means, plus $256 \times 64$ entries for Codebook A and $256 \times 8$ entries for Codebook B. This is significantly smaller than the original uncompressed volume [S1, unofficial].
