 ## Background
-This method was developed as part of a system for real-time rendering of compressed time-varying volume data. It addresses the bottleneck of data exchange between main memory and GPU memory by moving the decoding process to the GPU. The approach uses Vector Quantization (VQ) with two codebooks (Codebook A for difference levels and Codebook B for detail levels) and stores the compressed data in GPU texture memory. The implementation utilized the Cg programming language to ensure portability between NVIDIA and ATI GPUs, as Cg could compile to GLSL for ATI hardware, unlike CUDA which was NVIDIA-specific at the time [S1, unofficial].
